That is _not_ the optimal strategy.  The optimal strategy 
(AFAIK) is:  Keep track of your luck as precisely as you 
can.  Pray only when your luck is 7 or 8.  That way, you 
won't be crowned, and have a maximum chance of getting 
a spellbook.  A good way to regain control of your luck 
is:  Do something which gains you negative luck, until 
you're sure that your luck is negative.  Don't do anything 
to decrease your alignment, however.  Then pray; this 
will sometimes reset your luck to 0 ('golden glow').  
If not, you can try 

a) hanging around waiting for next prayer, 

b) sacrifice small things and wait for the 
'reconciliation' message; this should set 
your luck to 0.  

Sacrificing corpses is a good way to alter 
your luck controllably; there are tables 
in the spoilers 

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/340/gems-340.html

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/pray.html

http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/experience-spoiler.html

which help to detail out how much luck you gained.  
A good way to decrease luck is e.g. jumping in 
Soko, or breaking mirrors.  

